/**
\fn std::optional<CollisionQueryHit> pdg::Scene::raycast(const Point& start, const Point& end, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Return the closest accepted segment hit.
Queries inspect current authoritative enabled attached Sprite, Part and Particle
colliders, including bodyless colliders, independently of cameras and contact
response. Available before stepping and while paused; call outside scene update/draw
traversal. Predicates must not mutate geometry, scene membership, results or timing,
or recursively query. Predicate failures propagate. Disposed scenes reject queries.

Single-hit C++ values and their copies retain their colliders independently.
Multiple-hit methods return a const reference to one scene-owned vector, valid
until the next query on that scene or disposal. Copy the vector and explicitly
retain collider references when keeping multiple-hit data longer. The vector uses
reusable storage; geometry snapshots and scratch storage can allocate.

A separate maxHits argument caps cast array overloads; CollisionQueryOptions.maxHits caps overlap results (default 16, range 0 to 1048576).
Other options select layerMask intersected with layer queryBits, explicit layers,
categoryMask, includeSensors, excludedColliders, excludedBodies and a synchronous
boolean predicate. Foreign/detached explicit layers throw. Zero/empty selection
matches nothing. Layers default to queryBits 1. queryBits are not serialized.

Hits use scene world coordinates and public shape IDs. Casts sort by travel distance,
collider ID then shape ID; overlaps sort by identity and expose only collider/shapeId.
Initial touching/overlap counts and returns zero distance/fraction/normal. Nearest
points use filled geometry: interior points return themselves at distance zero.
No truncation flag is exposed for multiple results. Finite coordinates and
nonnegative finite radii/distances are required; boxes must have positive dimensions.

\param start World segment start.
\param end World segment end.
\param options Optional scene selection.
\return Closest retained hit, or std::nullopt on a miss.
\note Attach searched layers to a live scene; no physics step is required.
\par Example
\code{.cpp}
pdg::CollisionQueryOptions options;
options.maxHits = 8;
const auto& hits = scene.raycast(pdg::Point(0, 50), pdg::Point(200, 50), 8, options);
for (const auto& hit : hits) { /* use hit.collider and hit.distance here */ }
// The next query invalidates the multiple-hit records above.
\endcode
*/
/**
\fn const std::vector<CollisionQueryHit>& pdg::Scene::raycast(const Point& start, const Point& end, uint32_t maxHits, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
\param start Segment start.
\param end Segment end.
\param maxHits Integer multiple-hit limit, 0 to 1048576.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Scene-owned vector, valid until the next query or disposal; empty on a miss.
*/
/**
\fn std::optional<CollisionQueryHit> pdg::Scene::sweepCircle(const Point& center, double radius, const Vector& delta, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
\param center Initial world center.
\param radius Finite nonnegative world radius.
\param delta World translation.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Closest retained hit or std::nullopt.
*/
/**
\fn const std::vector<CollisionQueryHit>& pdg::Scene::sweepCircle(const Point& center, double radius, const Vector& delta, uint32_t maxHits, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
\param center Initial world center.
\param radius Finite nonnegative world radius.
\param delta World translation.
\param maxHits Integer multiple-hit limit, 0 to 1048576.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Scene-owned vector, valid until the next query or disposal; empty on a miss.
*/
/**
\fn const std::vector<CollisionQueryHit>& pdg::Scene::overlapPoint(const Point& point, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
\param point World point.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Scene-owned vector, valid until the next query or disposal; empty on a miss.
*/
/**
\fn const std::vector<CollisionQueryHit>& pdg::Scene::overlapCircle(const Point& center, double radius, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
\param center World center.
\param radius Finite nonnegative world radius.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Scene-owned vector, valid until the next query or disposal; empty on a miss.
*/
/**
\fn const std::vector<CollisionQueryHit>& pdg::Scene::overlapBox(const RotatedRect& box, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
\param box Positive-size oriented world box.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Scene-owned vector, valid until the next query or disposal; empty on a miss.
*/
/**
\fn const std::vector<CollisionQueryHit>& pdg::Scene::overlapCapsule(const Point& start, const Point& end, double radius, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
\param start First cap center.
\param end Second cap center.
\param radius Finite nonnegative world radius.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Scene-owned vector, valid until the next query or disposal; empty on a miss.
*/
/**
\fn std::optional<CollisionQueryHit> pdg::Scene::nearestPoint(const Point& point, double maxDistance, const CollisionQueryOptions& options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry.
Find the closest point on filled geometry within maxDistance. Inside a shape,
return the input point with distance zero.
\param point World search point.
\param maxDistance Finite nonnegative inclusive search distance.
\param options Optional scene selection; maxHits caps multiple results.
\return Closest retained hit or std::nullopt.
*/
